/target
/dist
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
/handoff.md
# A CANONICAL blend is canonical BY LOCATION: `assets/<id>/<id>.blend` — one directory under
# `assets/`, named after that directory, which is where the trio rule looks for a source and where
# every derived path is cut from. Those are tracked (LFS, `.gitattributes`), because the committed
# derivative — the trio of view glb, sim glb and certificate — must travel with the source it was
# cut from or nothing can re-cut it; the shared material library at
# `assets/materials/materials.blend` has that shape too, and every tank blend links its substances
# out of it. A second vehicle is tracked by that rule and edits nothing here. Everything else
# blend-shaped is local authoring scratch: a blend anywhere else, Blender's own `.blend1` rolling
# backup, and the hand-made `.bak` snapshots a session leaves beside it.
#
# THE NEGATION BELOW IS BROADER THAN THAT LAW and cannot be narrowed: a gitignore pattern has no way
# to say "named after its own directory", so `!assets/*/*.blend` unignores every blend in an asset's
# directory, `assets/tiger_1/scratch.blend` included. The canonical shape is stated where it is
# executable — `assets_blend_shape` in `scripts/hooks/pushed_assets.sh`, which refuses a push, and
# the CI assets job, which refuses the commit.
*.blend
!assets/*/*.blend
*.blend1
*.bak

# Scratch output of a hand-run texture bake. The BAKED glb is the tracked one; an asset ships one
# glb and this line makes a second one impossible to commit by accident.
*.mipped.glb

# Firecrawl research scratch (web search/scrape cache)
.firecrawl/

# Cloudflare wrangler local cache
.wrangler/
__pycache__/
